# What NOT to copy into the image.
#
# Without this file `COPY . .` bakes in .venv — a Windows virtualenv roughly a
# hundred times larger than the application it supports, which cannot run on
# the Linux base image anyway.
#
# Note this file is NOT the same as .gcloudignore: Docker reads this one when
# building, gcloud reads that one when staging source for Cloud Build. Both
# exist, and both have to list .venv, or whichever is missing lets it back in.
# Render builds this Dockerfile directly, so only this file applies there.
.venv/
.venv-*/
venv/
build/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/

# Local-only state and secrets. .env points at the emulator; shipping it would
# have production quietly try to reach a database on someone's laptop.
.env
.env.*
var/
*.log

# The test suite needs the Firestore emulator, which does not exist in the
# image. Nothing runs it there.
tests/
